# same.mask - what tests/toolhelp/thcmp.py leaves out when it compares
# the probe's log with Microsoft's TOOLHELP against its log with w16's on
# the same system (tests/toolhelp/thcase.sh, parts ref286, ref386, ref3):
# two boots, so only what depends on the boot itself. Nothing of
# TOOLHELP's answers is left out: section d compares both TOOLHELPs in one
# session, structure for structure, without a mask.
#
# the number of blocks, modules and classes section d went through: the
# global heap is not laid out alike in two boots (the two TOOLHELPs' own
# segments differ in size)
^d walk (ALL|LRU|FREE): [0-9]+ entries$
# the order KERNEL frees a library's code segments in (THD's 2, 3, 4):
# under 3.1's KRNL286 it changed from one boot to the next, the same
# KERNEL, in what it reported to a raw hook (section n) as in the
# FREESEGs: it seems to follow where the segments are in the global heap
# (UNVERIFIED)
s/^raw ([0-9]+): 52 bx=seg[2-4] /raw \1: 52 bx=seg* /
s/FREESEG THD\.seg[2-4] /FREESEG THD.seg* /
# likewise the order a program's segments are freed in when it ends
s/FREESEG (THC\.seg[0-9]|M:THC|child\.dg\.s|\?) task=/FREESEG (THC) task=/
